<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Segestes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Segestes was a nobleman of the Cherusci in the early 1st century CE and a leading supporter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He warned the governor Varus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a>' plans before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest">Battle of the Teutoburg Forest</a> in 9 CE, but was ignored. His daughter Thusnelda married Arminius against his will; in 15 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> relieved Segestes from a siege by Arminius, and Thusnelda was taken to Rome as a captive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/segestes.jpg" alt="Segestes" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin West · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benjamin_West_(1738-1820)_-_The_Wife_of_Arminius_brought_captive_to_Germanicus_-_RCIN_405683_-_Royal_Collection.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
